---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — K팝 관심도. (/kpop-attention)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 사장님 지시(2026-08-05): 「k팝 등에 관심이 많은 **해외 대상**이다」.
 * 그런데 지면 열다섯 장 중 음악은 `/exports` 한 장뿐이고 그것도 **수출 금액**이었다.
 * 사람이 K팝을 검색해 들어올 자리가 한 곳도 없었다. 그 자리다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 관심은 인기가 아니다 ────────────────────────────────────
 * 조회수는 좋은 일로도 나쁜 일로도 오른다. **「인기 순위」라고 쓰지 않는다.**
 * 급상승은 총량과 **따로** 놓는다 — 섞으면 스캔들이 인기로 읽힌다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 배우가 섞여 있다. 빼지 않고 표시한다 ────────────────────
 * 위키데이터가 배우 여럿에게 「가수」 직업도 달아 두었다. 지수도 차은우도 실제로 둘 다다.
 * 우리가 가를 일이 아니다. 다만 그대로 두면 **개인 1위가 소지섭**이 되어 읽는 사람을 속인다.
 * 편수로 7.9% 인데 **조회수로는 27.1%** 다 — 두 수를 다 내고, 뺀 목록을 **나란히** 둔다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 그룹과 개인을 같은 자로 재지 않는다 ────────────────────
 * 그룹 문서 하나에 멤버 여럿의 관심이 모인다. 한 표에 섞으면 그룹이 커 보이는 게 아니라
 * **잘못 보인다.** 나눠 놓고 왜 다른지를 적는다.
 *
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production 승인 전이다.
 * ⛔ 사진을 쓰지 않는다. 우리가 만든 숫자만 쓴다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-kpop.json';

const TITLE = 'Who the English-speaking world looks up when it looks up K-pop';
const DESC =
  `Thirty days of English Wikipedia page views for every Korean musician and group with an article — `
  + `${data.roster.toLocaleString()} of them. Measured, not voted on, and we say what the ranking cannot tell you.`;

const 만 = (v: number) => v.toLocaleString('en-US');
const 날 = (s: string) => `${s.slice(0, 4)}-${s.slice(4, 6)}-${s.slice(6, 8)}`;
const 기간 = `${날(data.period.slice(0, 8))} to ${날(data.period.slice(9))}`;
const 겹 = data.actorOverlap;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: `${날(data.period.slice(0, 8))}/${날(data.period.slice(9))}`,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/kpop-attention">
  <h1>Who the English-speaking world looks up when it looks up K-pop</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every Korean musician and musical group with an English Wikipedia article — {만(data.roster)} of
    them — and how many times each article was opened by a person over {data.days} days,
    {' '}{기간}. Nobody voted. We counted.
  </p>

  <section class="stats">
    <div><b>{만(data.roster)}</b><span>acts measured</span></div>
    <div><b>{(data.totalViews / 1e6).toFixed(1)}m</b><span>page views in {data.days} days</span></div>
    <div><b>{data.concentration[1].sharePc}%</b><span>held by the top ten</span></div>
    <div><b>{data.groups.n}</b><span>groups · {만(data.people.n)} individuals</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="warn">
    <h2>Read this before the tables</h2>
    <p class="body">
      <b>Attention is not popularity.</b> A page climbs for good news and for bad, for a comeback and
      for a court date. We report the count and not the reason, and nothing here is a ranking of who is
      liked.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      <b>{겹.n} of these {만(data.roster)} acts are also in our actors list</b> — Wikidata records
      "singer" among their occupations and they are also working actors. That is {겹.nPc}% of the
      names but <b>{겹.viewsPc}% of the views</b>. We have not removed them, because Jisoo and
      Cha Eun-woo really are both. We show the list both ways instead.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Groups</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      {data.groups.n} groups, {만(data.groups.views)} views, {만(data.groups.mean)} on average.
    </p>
    <ol class="rank">
      {data.topGroups.map((r) => (
        <li>
          <span class="bar" style={`--w:${(r.total / data.topGroups[0].total) * 100}%`}></span>
          <span class="nm">{r.name}</span>
          <span class="meta"><b>{만(r.total)}</b> views · {만(r.daily)}/day · peak {날(r.peakDay)}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Individuals</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      {만(data.people.n)} people, {만(data.people.views)} views, {만(data.people.mean)} on average.
      Names marked <i>also an actor</i> appear in our <a href="/actors">actors list</a> as well.
    </p>
    <ol class="rank">
      {data.topPeople.map((r) => (
        <li>
          <span class="bar" style={`--w:${(r.total / data.topPeople[0].total) * 100}%`}></span>
          <span class="nm">
            {r.name}
            {r.alsoActor && <span class="tag"> also an actor</span>}
          </span>
          <span class="meta"><b>{만(r.total)}</b> views · {만(r.daily)}/day · peak {날(r.peakDay)}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="note">
      The top of that list is not what most readers expect from a K-pop page, and that is the point of
      showing it. Take out everyone who is also in the actors list and the same thirty days read
      differently:
    </p>
    <ol class="rank tight">
      {data.topMusicOnly.slice(0, 10).map((r) => (
        <li>
          <span class="bar" style={`--w:${(r.total / data.topMusicOnly[0].total) * 100}%`}></span>
          <span class="nm">{r.name}</span>
          <span class="meta"><b>{만(r.total)}</b> views</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="note">
      Neither list is the correct one. The first is everyone Wikidata calls a Korean musician; the
      second is the part of that group who do not also act. Which one you want depends on the question
      you are asking, so we publish both rather than choose for you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Attention is concentrated, but less than viewing is</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Top</th><th>Views</th><th>Share of all {data.days}-day attention</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.concentration.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{c.top === 1 ? 'Top 1' : `Top ${c.top}`}</td>
              <td>{만(c.views)}</td><td class="tot">{c.sharePc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The single most looked-up act holds {data.concentration[0].sharePc}% of the attention across
      {' '}{만(data.roster)} acts. On <a href="/watched">Netflix's global chart</a> the single biggest Korean
      title holds a fifth of five years of viewing. Both are concentrated; the audience for music
      spreads its attention more widely than the chart spreads its hours. These are different
      measures on different populations, and we are placing them beside each other rather than
      claiming one explains the other.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Rising fastest</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Last seven days against the first seven of the window. Acts below 300 views this week are
      excluded — ten views becoming forty is a fourfold rise and means nothing.
    </p>
    <ol class="rank">
      {data.rising.slice(0, 10).map((r) => (
        <li>
          <span class="nm">
            {r.name}
            {r.alsoActor && <span class="tag"> also an actor</span>}
          </span>
          <span class="meta">×<b>{r.rise}</b> · {만(r.last7)} views this week</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="note">
      <b>This column is kept apart from the totals on purpose.</b> A sharp rise is a thing that
      happened, not a thing that is good. Merged into one ranking it would read as popularity, and we
      have no way to tell you which of these is a comeback and which is a headline nobody wanted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/kpop-attention" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Wikimedia</b> — {data.source}. Human traffic only; bots and spiders are excluded by the API itself.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Who is in the list, and why we did not choose.</b> {data.rosterSource} We did not pick
        favourites — a list we assembled by hand would be a list of our own taste. All
        {' '}{data.rosterQueries} queries returned, so nothing is missing because a query failed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>{만(data.measured)} of {만(data.roster)} were measured.</b> {data.notFound} had no article
        under the name Wikidata gives, and {data.fetchFailed} could not be fetched. A missing article
        is not zero views — it is a name we could not look up, and it is counted separately for that
        reason.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Groups and individuals are not on the same scale.</b> One group article collects the
        attention of everyone in it, so a group's number and a person's number do not mean the same
        thing. That is why they are in two tables and never added together.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>English Wikipedia only.</b> This measures the English-speaking world, which is who this
        publication is for. It says nothing about attention in Korean, Japanese, Spanish or Indonesian.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Thirty days is thirty days.</b> A comeback, a tour date or a controversy inside the window
        moves an act a long way. Nothing here is a career total.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.7rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.25; }
  .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .sub { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; line-height: 1.65; }
  .body { font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }

  .stats { display: grid; gap: .6rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
  @media (min-width: 34rem) { .stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
  .stats > div { background: var(--card); border-radius: 8px; padding: .8rem .9rem; }
  .stats b { display: block; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.01em;
             font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stats span { display: block; font-size: .74rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .2rem; line-height: 1.4; }

  /* 경고 절은 표보다 먼저 읽혀야 한다 — 눈에 띄되 요란하지 않게 */
  .warn { background: var(--card); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; }
  .warn h2 { margin-bottom: .5rem; }

  .rank { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .rank li { position: relative; padding: .5rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .rank.tight li { padding: .35rem .6rem; }
  .bar { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: var(--w); background: var(--accent);
         opacity: .13; border-radius: 4px; }
  .nm { position: relative; display: block; font-weight: 700; font-size: .93rem; }
  .meta { position: relative; display: block; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .15rem;
          font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .tag { font-weight: 400; font-size: .74rem; color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; }
  th, td { padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right;
           white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th { font-size: .71rem; letter-spacing: .03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
       font-weight: 700; }
  th:first-child, td.nm { text-align: left; }
  td.tot { font-weight: 700; }

  .src ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .src li { margin: .5rem 0; }
  .src b { color: var(--ink); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
